# SPEC GOLDEN — hand-derived from css-flexbox-1 §5.1 (flex-direction) and §9.5
# before the code existed, never regenerated.
#
# `row-reverse` does not reorder the document and does not change the
# arithmetic: it points the main axis the other way. **Main-start becomes the
# container's right edge**, so the first item in order-modified document order
# is the rightmost one, `flex-start` packs right, and every offset §9.5
# computes from main-start is subtracted from the right edge instead of added
# to the left. That mapping is the whole of what this direction costs — the
# same placement pass produces both rows.
#
# The boxes are still listed in main-axis order, first item first, which is why
# x *descends* down each row below. Order-modified document order is what the
# layout tree holds (M9.6, `order`), and the DOM is untouched.
#
# Three `flex: 0 0 160px` (= 20 cell) items in 80 cells again: 60 used, 20 to
# place.
#
# Row 1 — `flex-start`. Lead 0, so item a sits *at* main-start:
#   a: 80 - 0 - 20 = 60,  b: 80 - 20 - 20 = 40,  c: 80 - 40 - 20 = 20.
#   The 20 spare cells are at main-end, which here is the left edge — the
#   mirror image of what `flex-start` leaves on a plain row.
#
# Row 2 — `space-between`: 20 cells over 2 inner slots, 10 each. Offsets from
#   main-start are 0, 30, 60, so
#   a: 80 - 0 - 20 = 60,  b: 80 - 30 - 20 = 30,  c: 80 - 60 - 20 = 0.
#   First item at main-start (the right edge), last at main-end (the left) —
#   the definition read in the direction the axis actually points.
#
# Row 3 — `gap: 1em` = 2 cells, `flex-start`. Reserved 4, free 16 at main-end.
#   Offsets 0, 22, 44, so
#   a: 60,  b: 80 - 22 - 20 = 38,  c: 80 - 44 - 20 = 16.
#
# Text inside an item is unaffected: a reversed main axis reverses the order of
# the boxes, not the direction the words in them run.
<html>  x=0 y=0 w=80 h=3
  <body>  x=0 y=0 w=80 h=3
    <div.row> flex row-reverse  x=0 y=0 w=80 h=1
      <div>  x=60 y=0 w=20 h=1
        anonymous  x=60 y=0 w=20 h=1
          line  x=60 y=0 w=20 h=1
            #text "a"  x=60 y=0 w=1 h=1
      <div>  x=40 y=0 w=20 h=1
        anonymous  x=40 y=0 w=20 h=1
          line  x=40 y=0 w=20 h=1
            #text "b"  x=40 y=0 w=1 h=1
      <div>  x=20 y=0 w=20 h=1
        anonymous  x=20 y=0 w=20 h=1
          line  x=20 y=0 w=20 h=1
            #text "c"  x=20 y=0 w=1 h=1
    <div.row.between> flex row-reverse  x=0 y=1 w=80 h=1
      <div>  x=60 y=1 w=20 h=1
        anonymous  x=60 y=1 w=20 h=1
          line  x=60 y=1 w=20 h=1
            #text "a"  x=60 y=1 w=1 h=1
      <div>  x=30 y=1 w=20 h=1
        anonymous  x=30 y=1 w=20 h=1
          line  x=30 y=1 w=20 h=1
            #text "b"  x=30 y=1 w=1 h=1
      <div>  x=0 y=1 w=20 h=1
        anonymous  x=0 y=1 w=20 h=1
          line  x=0 y=1 w=20 h=1
            #text "c"  x=0 y=1 w=1 h=1
    <div.row.gap> flex row-reverse  x=0 y=2 w=80 h=1
      <div>  x=60 y=2 w=20 h=1
        anonymous  x=60 y=2 w=20 h=1
          line  x=60 y=2 w=20 h=1
            #text "a"  x=60 y=2 w=1 h=1
      <div>  x=38 y=2 w=20 h=1
        anonymous  x=38 y=2 w=20 h=1
          line  x=38 y=2 w=20 h=1
            #text "b"  x=38 y=2 w=1 h=1
      <div>  x=16 y=2 w=20 h=1
        anonymous  x=16 y=2 w=20 h=1
          line  x=16 y=2 w=20 h=1
            #text "c"  x=16 y=2 w=1 h=1
